WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:04.549 --> 00:00:09.870
A few years back, news headlines mentioned
names like BT COTTON, BT

00:00:09.870 --> 00:00:12.450
BRINJAL and so on!

00:00:12.450 --> 00:00:15.809
And even the markets were flooded with them!

00:00:15.809 --> 00:00:17.590
Any idea what these are?

00:00:17.590 --> 00:00:18.910
That’s right!

00:00:18.910 --> 00:00:24.759
These are genetically modified crops,
abbreviated as GM plants.

00:00:24.759 --> 00:00:27.890
We have heard about them several times!

00:00:27.890 --> 00:00:30.529
These
plants are the modified versions of the original

00:00:30.529 --> 00:00:33.620
variety.

00:00:33.620 --> 00:00:37.850
Modifications in the
plants add many advantages like greater yield,

00:00:37.850 --> 00:00:42.420
insect resistance, nutritional
value and so on!

00:00:42.420 --> 00:00:45.109
But how do we modify the plants?

00:00:45.109 --> 00:00:47.920
How is the transformation carried out?

00:00:47.920 --> 00:00:52.960
For
that, each plant part acts as a mini laboratory!

00:00:52.960 --> 00:00:56.399
Several experiments are carried
out on EACH PART.

00:00:56.399 --> 00:01:00.210
At the end of many such experiments, finally
a product is

00:01:00.210 --> 00:01:04.409
achieved that has the desired characters!

00:01:04.409 --> 00:01:08.940
So in order to make useful products, we modify
the crops.

00:01:08.940 --> 00:01:12.330
But in order to
modify them, we need to study each and every

00:01:12.330 --> 00:01:15.870
part of plants in detail.

00:01:15.870 --> 00:01:20.840
In this, and in the upcoming sessions, let
us learn and understand each part of

00:01:20.840 --> 00:01:23.370
the plants in detail.

00:01:23.370 --> 00:01:25.050
And where do we begin with?

00:01:25.050 --> 00:01:27.090
The top or the bottom?

00:01:27.090 --> 00:01:31.090
Let’s toss and choose
which part to begin with!

00:01:31.090 --> 00:01:34.790
If it’s heads, we begin with the shoot,
and if it’s tails,

00:01:34.790 --> 00:01:35.980
we begin with the roots!

00:01:35.980 --> 00:01:38.380
So let’s get started!

00:01:38.380 --> 00:01:41.850
Here we go!

00:01:41.850 --> 00:01:43.310
We have got tails!

00:01:43.310 --> 00:01:45.940
So now let us begin with studying a typical
plant beginning

00:01:45.940 --> 00:01:48.650
with the roots and moving to the shoots!

00:01:48.650 --> 00:01:53.670
Let us start our understanding of the
roots first!

00:01:53.670 --> 00:01:58.200
There are three major areas of study that
we need to carry out!

00:01:58.200 --> 00:02:01.750
First is the
TYPE of roots, second is the various REGIONS

00:02:01.750 --> 00:02:03.710
or PARTS of the roots.

00:02:03.710 --> 00:02:06.770
And lastly
we will study the various MODIFICATIONS of

00:02:06.770 --> 00:02:07.770
the roots!

00:02:07.770 --> 00:02:08.770
Four topics to be discussed:
- Types of roots

00:02:08.770 --> 00:02:09.770
- Regions of a typical root
- Modifications of roots

00:02:09.770 --> 00:02:12.120
Let us begin with the types of roots first!

00:02:12.120 --> 00:02:16.200
Here we see a carrot and an onion in the soil.

00:02:16.200 --> 00:02:22.010
If we uproot both the plants, where can you
locate the roots in both of these?

00:02:22.010 --> 00:02:25.960
Well, this complete structure of a carrot
is like a root!

00:02:25.960 --> 00:02:26.960
Yes!

00:02:26.960 --> 00:02:30.950
In case of carrot,
this complete structure is the main root which

00:02:30.950 --> 00:02:33.420
is edible!

00:02:33.420 --> 00:02:37.410
On the other hand, in
case of this onion, we find these small, bunch

00:02:37.410 --> 00:02:39.700
like structures.

00:02:39.700 --> 00:02:41.370
These are its
roots!

00:02:41.370 --> 00:02:44.180
So can we say that there are two major types
of roots?

00:02:44.180 --> 00:02:49.750
Well, there are various types of roots found
throughout the plant kingdom!

00:02:49.750 --> 00:02:51.990
But
we will restrict ourselves to three major

00:02:51.990 --> 00:02:53.260
types!

00:02:53.260 --> 00:02:57.330
The first one is the category of carrots!

00:02:57.330 --> 00:03:00.930
These types of roots are called
Taproots!

00:03:00.930 --> 00:03:04.930
The second type is the one in which there
are bunch like structures.

00:03:04.930 --> 00:03:07.790
The ones found in this onion!

00:03:07.790 --> 00:03:11.070
These are called the fibrous roots.

00:03:11.070 --> 00:03:14.180
And the last
type, which we are yet to discuss, is called

00:03:14.180 --> 00:03:17.380
as adventitious roots.

00:03:17.380 --> 00:03:19.900
This type
involves the roots which arise from other

00:03:19.900 --> 00:03:24.190
parts of the plant body, and not the
main roots, below the stem!

00:03:24.190 --> 00:03:26.090
Don’t get confused!

00:03:26.090 --> 00:03:30.520
Let us understand each type
better

00:03:30.520 --> 00:03:34.290
Taproot system is the one in which there is
a single root which is the primary

00:03:34.290 --> 00:03:36.850
root that anchors the plant.

00:03:36.850 --> 00:03:40.340
The one seen in this case.

00:03:40.340 --> 00:03:44.950
There are several secondary and tertiary roots;
that is these smaller root like

00:03:44.950 --> 00:03:48.060
structures which arise from the primary root!

00:03:48.060 --> 00:03:53.170
The primary root has the
tendency to grow deeper in the soil.

00:03:53.170 --> 00:03:57.790
Usually, dicot plants exhibit the taproot
system.

00:03:57.790 --> 00:04:01.099
The second type is that of the fibrous root
system.

00:04:01.099 --> 00:04:04.490
This type does not contain a
single primary root.

00:04:04.490 --> 00:04:08.040
Rather, many smaller roots come together to
form a bunch

00:04:08.040 --> 00:04:10.380
like structure.

00:04:10.380 --> 00:04:13.980
These roots usually do not grow too deep,
unless the tree is very

00:04:13.980 --> 00:04:15.750
huge!

00:04:15.750 --> 00:04:19.139
And what kind of plants exhibit this type
of system?

00:04:19.139 --> 00:04:20.819
That’s right!

00:04:20.819 --> 00:04:24.870
Monocots usually have the fibrous root system!

00:04:24.870 --> 00:04:27.669
Now comes the last type from our list.

00:04:27.669 --> 00:04:31.090
That is the adventitious root system!

00:04:31.090 --> 00:04:35.379
This type deals with the roots that unusually
originate from the other parts of

00:04:35.379 --> 00:04:41.939
plants like the branches, stem, leaves or
even some old woody roots at times.

00:04:41.939 --> 00:04:45.800
Have you ever seen a huge Banyan tree?

00:04:45.800 --> 00:04:49.180
Any idea what these string like structures
are?

00:04:49.180 --> 00:04:52.080
Well these are actually the
ROOTS!

00:04:52.080 --> 00:04:53.080
Yes!

00:04:53.080 --> 00:04:57.460
A banyan tree like this one has these string
like structures.

00:04:57.460 --> 00:05:01.180
These
are the prop roots which arise from the branches!

00:05:01.180 --> 00:05:06.850
These roots are called aerial
roots which are a type of adventitious roots.

00:05:06.850 --> 00:05:12.650
As we can see here, the roots
arise from the aerial parts, the branches.

00:05:12.650 --> 00:05:14.430
They grow from above the ground.

00:05:14.430 --> 00:05:18.999
And they firmly adhere to the ground, giving
the huge tree a proper structural

00:05:18.999 --> 00:05:21.190
support as well!

00:05:21.190 --> 00:05:24.740
Note that a banyan tree does have a proper
root system under

00:05:24.740 --> 00:05:25.740
the ground.

00:05:25.740 --> 00:05:29.830
The adventitious roots are just additional
ones that help in making

00:05:29.830 --> 00:05:34.240
a few systems work efficiently in the plant
body.

00:05:34.240 --> 00:05:38.389
This is one example of
adventitious roots.

00:05:38.389 --> 00:05:42.509
Now before moving ahead with the next section,
let us revise the types of

00:05:42.509 --> 00:05:44.539
roots once.

00:05:44.539 --> 00:05:47.319
The first type is that of the taproots.

00:05:47.319 --> 00:05:51.800
This type has a single, long
primary root system and smaller, secondary

00:05:51.800 --> 00:05:57.139
and tertiary roots arising from it,
just like in case of carrots.

00:05:57.139 --> 00:05:59.939
The second type is the fibrous roots.

00:05:59.939 --> 00:06:03.419
In this type,
several smaller roots come together to form

00:06:03.419 --> 00:06:08.270
a single bunch like structure, just
like in case of onion roots.

00:06:08.270 --> 00:06:12.449
Lastly, we have the adventitious root system.

00:06:12.449 --> 00:06:18.150
Here, the roots arise from different parts
of the plant like the stem, branches,

00:06:18.150 --> 00:06:19.400
leaves and so on.

00:06:19.400 --> 00:06:23.280
The prop roots of the banyan tree can be considered
as a

00:06:23.280 --> 00:06:26.849
good example of the adventitious roots!

00:06:26.849 --> 00:06:30.389
This was about the types of roots.

00:06:30.389 --> 00:06:35.020
We shall have a look at the next topic that
is regions or the parts of the roots in

00:06:35.020 --> 00:06:37.139
the upcoming video!

00:06:37.139 --> 00:06:39.680
Do subscribe to our channel to get updated
about the

00:06:39.680 --> 00:06:42.110
launch of our next video!

